      "writtenOn": "2024-05-31T15:50:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t agree with the introduction of this new log helper, though we can discuss about the need for a non fatal checker.\n\nOne of the main goals for adding the log library was to unify log behaviors, and make logs more deterministic. In particular I decided to remove everything that made use of NDEBUG to force similar behaviors between production and release builds.\n\nAdding assert_that_softly goes against this as the behavior is conditional on the platform.\n\nNow it might be useful to have a soft version of assert_that, e.g. check_that,\ndepending on how you plan on using it.",
      "revId": "3f4f7faa5ad084e7aa7f65ffdfa86a313bc42d6f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "22853a1f_cd105e36",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1599263
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-31T16:39:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the additional context. Simply having assert_that_softly could meet our need, I still hit unexpected core dump (not abort) with unexpected HCI events.\n\ncheck_that sounds interesting, we can revisit it when there\u0027s valid use case.",
      "parentUuid": "a7d441dd_88396951",
      "revId": "3f4f7faa5ad084e7aa7f65ffdfa86a313bc42d6f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6b446d9a_d75c7279",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-31T17:25:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In that case I think it is more appropriate to remove the specific asserts that have been triggered by Floss, and replace them with manual (not check_that) checks + error logs.\n\nIf an assert is used to check a controller behavior, then we must make sure that the behavior is standard.",
      "parentUuid": "22853a1f_cd105e36",
      "revId": "3f4f7faa5ad084e7aa7f65ffdfa86a313bc42d6f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
